(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Generators (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.4-§7.5; the survey's PYS7 (a); PY5d): a generator, a"] [4 1 "// coroutine and an async generator are the frame of their function's call kept between resumptions."] [5 1 "// The call makes the object without running the frame (newGeneratorHook); each resumption runs the"] [6 1 "// kept frame by (*Thread).run as an entry frame, a yield (yield-value, or yield-from delegating)"] [7 1 "// returns from the loop with Frame.Suspended set, and the frame's handler table sees an exception"] [8 1 "// thrown in at the instruction it is suspended at (Lasti). CPython's Objects/genobject.c and the"] [9 1 "// YIELD_VALUE, SEND and RETURN_GENERATOR parts of Python/bytecodes.c."] [26 1 "// Generator is a generator, a coroutine or an async generator (CPython's PyGenObject, PyCoroObject"] [27 1 "// and PyAsyncGenObject): the kept frame of its function's call."] [30 18 "// nil once finished (gi_frame None)"] [32 18 "// __name__, the function's"] [33 18 "// __qualname__"] [34 18 "// run at least once (FRAME_CREATED otherwise)"] [35 18 "// gi_running"] [36 2 "// handled is the exception the frame is handling while it is suspended (gi_exc_state), nil when none."] [38 2 "// ext is what few generators have, nil until one is set (every generator allocates the rest)"] [40 2 "// the async generator's state (PyAsyncGenObject)"] [41 20 "// ag_closed"] [42 20 "// ag_running_async: an asend or athrow awaits it"] [43 20 "// ag_hooks_inited: sys's firstiter hook called (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200)"] [44 2 "// finTracked: its finalization is due at its death (finalize.go's workGen, queue 218)"] [46 2 "// finPending: in finalize.go's pendingGens, tracked at the flush when still not finished"] [48 2 "// madeAt, madeF, madeL: callSeq, the calling frame's address and its instruction when made (stampGen; queue 297)"] [52 2 "// exposed: handed out by f_generator (queue 297: then held by more than the value stack)"] [56 1 "// genExt is a generator's rare fields."] [58 2 "// origin is cr_origin: the frames that created a coroutine while origin tracking was on, nil otherwise"] [60 2 "// finalizer is sys's asyncgen finalizer hook at its first use (ag_origin_or_finalizer), nil when none"] [62 2 "// name, qualname: the objects assigned to __name__ and __qualname__, nil until then"] [66 1 "// more is g's rare fields, made when absent."] [84 1 "// newGenerator is a call's object of a function whose code is a generator's, a coroutine's or an"] [85 1 "// async generator's: f bound, not run."] [98 3 "// a coroutine never awaited warns at its death (_PyGen_Finalize; queue 218): tracked only if still not started"] [99 3 "// when the pending list is flushed (most are awaited at once)"] [107 1 "// genThrow is an exception thrown into a suspended frame: the resumption runs the frame's yield-value or yield-from"] [108 1 "// again (its PC set back to Lasti), which finds it here and raises it there, so the frame's handlers see it at the"] [109 1 "// suspension point. Its delegate has had it by then (_gen_throw, throwArgs). One thread runs at a time, and the frame's"] [110 1 "// first instruction run is that one."] [116 1 "// genSuspendedAt is the operation f is suspended at, when it is."] [124 1 "// yieldFrom is the delegate the generator is suspended in (gi_yieldfrom), or nil."] [132 1 "// resume runs g with v sent into it (exc nil) or exc raised in it (gen_send_ex2; closing: gen_close's, silent on an"] [133 1 "// exhausted coroutine): the value it yields (yielded non-nil), or the value it returns (returned, the generator"] [134 1 "// finished), or what it raises (err; a StopIteration raised in it is a RuntimeError, PEP 479)."] [155 4 "// raised at its RESUME: its frame in the traceback, the generator finished"] [170 2 "// the generator's own exception slot over the resuming level's (gi_exc_state pushed on the exc_info stack)"] [188 3 "// a generator suspended where a handler can see close()'s GeneratorExit is closed at its death (queue 218)"] [197 15 "// an exhausted generator's frame has no caller"] [205 1 "// stopIterationError is PEP 479's RuntimeError for a StopIteration (or, in an async generator, a"] [206 1 "// StopAsyncIteration) raised out of g's frame: its cause and context the exception, its traceback g's"] [207 1 "// frame's entry (CPython raises it in the frame, INTRINSIC_STOPITERATION_ERROR)."] [231 1 "// newStopIteration is StopIteration(v), with no arguments when v is None (gen_send_ex's)."] [239 1 "// stopIterationValue is a raised StopIteration's value (_PyGen_FetchStopIterationValue), ok false when"] [240 1 "// err is not one."] [252 1 "// isRaised is err a raised exception of type typ (or a subtype)."] [258 1 "// send is g.send(v): what it yields, or StopIteration with what it returns."] [270 1 "// throwRaised is gen_send_ex with an exception set: err raised in g's frame (a Go error that is no exception as it is)."] [279 1 "// excMatches is PyErr_GivenExceptionMatches of a class or an instance."] [287 1 "// throwArgs is _gen_throw: typ, val and tb as given (nil: not given), first to the delegate; closeOnGenExit false is"] [288 1 "// an async generator's aclose and athrow, whose GeneratorExit is thrown into the delegate. An error in the arguments"] [289 1 "// leaves g suspended."] [308 5 "// the frame linked into the stack, for complete backtraces"] [339 2 "// throw_here"] [364 1 "// normalizeException is PyErr_NormalizeException of a class and a value: the instance, or the exception making it"] [365 1 "// raised (which takes its place)."] [391 1 "// genThrowMethod is gen_throw: the arguments' count and deprecation, then _gen_throw."] [414 1 "// throw is g.throw(...)."] [426 1 "// close is g.close() (gen_close): GeneratorExit thrown in, or what closing its delegate raised; its return value when"] [427 1 "// it returns."] [465 1 "// genSendTo is a send into an iterator delegated to (SEND): a generator's or coroutine's resume, else"] [466 1 "// __next__ when v is None, else its send method; yielded non-nil, or the value it returned (a"] [467 1 "// StopIteration's, or None at an iterator's end)."] [472 40 "// FutureIter_am_send: no StopIteration made"] [476 50 "// PyIter_Send: tp_iternext when it has one"] [496 1 "// genCloseIter closes a delegate (gen_close_iter): a generator's or coroutine's close, else its close method when it"] [497 1 "// has one."] [515 1 "// asyncGenWrapped is a value an async generator yields (CPython's _PyAsyncGenWrappedValue): its asend"] [516 1 "// and athrow see it apart from the values its awaits yield to the event loop."] [521 1 "// opYieldValue is yield-value: the value popped and yielded (wrapped in an async generator), f kept"] [522 1 "// suspended; resumed, the value sent is on the stack (pushed by resume), or an exception thrown in is"] [523 1 "// raised here."] [539 1 "// chainStackItem is _PyErr_ChainStackItem (gen_send_ex2 with an exception, queue 223): an exception thrown into a"] [540 1 "// generator's frame takes the exception being handled as its __context__ (_PyErr_SetObject's chaining) when the"] [541 1 "// generator's own exception state, pushed at its resumption, holds one."] [550 1 "// opYieldFrom is yield-from ([receiver value] -> its return value): CPython's SEND, YIELD_VALUE and"] [551 1 "// END_SEND loop as one operation. Each value the receiver yields suspends f with the instruction run"] [552 1 "// again on resumption (PC set back to it), the receiver kept below and the sent value pushed on it."] [557 3 "// CLEANUP_THROW: a StopIteration is the delegate's end, its value this expression's; anything else is raised here"] [560 11 "// the placeholder resume pushed"] [579 54 "// the delegate's end: STOP_ITERATION, or RAISE (queue 219t)"] [590 1 "// opGetYieldFromIter is get-yield-from-iter: a generator or a coroutine as it is (a coroutine only in a"] [591 1 "// coroutine's code), else iter(o)."] [610 1 "// genMethods are the methods of the types of PY5d's files, put into their dictionaries by d5Ready"] [611 1 "// (lazily: a dictionary's keys need str's hash, which str.go's init sets after these files' inits)."] [618 1 "// d5Method declares a method of a type of PY5d's: name in t's dictionary as a built-in method."] [629 1 "// d5Ready fills the dictionaries of PY5d's types with their methods, once (each of their GetAttr"] [630 1 "// slots and operations calls it first)."] [651 1 "// d5GetAttr is the GetAttr slot of PY5d's types: their methods ready, then extra (attributes not in"] [652 1 "// the dictionary), then object's lookup."] [665 1 "// d5Args checks a method's argument count: between min and max positional, no keywords."] [681 1 "// coroOriginDepth is sys.set_coroutine_origin_tracking_depth's depth (0: off)."] [684 1 "// coroOrigin is compute_cr_origin: (filename, lineno, function name) of the creating frame and up to depth-1 of its"] [685 1 "// callers, innermost first."] [701 1 "// genRepr is \"<KIND object QUALNAME at 0x...>\", the address an identity number."] [708 1 "// genGetSets declares the attributes of a generator, coroutine or async generator (prefix gi_, cr_ or ag_; delegate"] [709 1 "// the attribute's name for gi_yieldfrom, cr_await, ag_await)."] [751 2 "// Next ends without the return value: the loop's for-iter and the abstract Next do not clear a"] [752 2 "// raised StopIteration yet (asked of PY5b and PY5c); __next__ and send raise it with the value."] [787 1 "// asStrSub is a str or a subclass's instance as its Str, else nil."] [795 1 "// nameObj is gi_name: the object set, a str subclass's kept."] [810 1 "// d5GenMethods declares send, throw and close of a generator or a coroutine."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[92 61] [126 38] [224 26] [281 23] [291 24] [303 45] [343 30] [348 25] [350 33] [368 27] [373 28] [380 28] [385 24] [400 145] [437 24] [469 31] [472 33] [480 44] [485 38] [499 31] [581 42] [594 28] [657 35] [689 18] [689 50] [692 54] [732 37] [758 62] [789 30] [813 54] [8